 tists together for informal presentations and conversation with an audienc
 e. This evening\, chaired by cultural historian Piero Scaruffi\, will feat
 ure these talks:\n\n- Roger Blandford (Stanford/Physics) on "Extreme Physi
 cs from Black Holes and Neutron Stars”\n\n- Stephen Quake (Stanford) on 
 "How AI is Changing Our Understanding of Cell Biology"\n\n- Hermann Nyuyko
 nge Kumbong (Stanford) on “Beyond Autoregression: Next-Concept Modeling
 ”\n\nThe art component will consist of a lunch-time Zoom conversation ab
 out the poet Fernando Pessoa with Portugal-based scholar Richard Zenith fo
 r which you can register at: L.A.S.E.R.: A conversation about poet Fernand
 o Pessoa - Stanford University\n\nRoger Blandford is the Director of the S
 imons Collaboration on Extreme Electrodynamics of Compact Sources at Stanf
 ord. His research interests include compact sources\, cosmic rays\, cosmol
 ogy\, and astrobiology. He is a Fellow of the Royal Society\, the American
  Academy of Arts and Sciences\, the American Physical Society and a Member
  of the National Academy of Sciences. He was awarded the 1998 AAS Heineman
  Prize \, the 2013 RAS Gold Medal\, the 2016 Crafoord Prize for Astronomy 
 and the 2020 Shaw Prize for Astronomy.\n\nHermann Nyuykonge Kumbong\, orig
